---
import CalcPage from '../../components/CalcPage.astro';
import Field from '../../components/Field.astro';
---

<CalcPage
  title="Creatinine clearance"
  kicker="Dosing"
  lede="Cockcroft-Gault estimates creatinine clearance from age, sex, weight and serum creatinine. The answer is in mL/min, the same units renal dosing tables use when they say “if CrCl is below…”."
  description="Estimate Cockcroft-Gault creatinine clearance from age, sex, serum creatinine, height and weight. Dosing weight is the lower of actual body weight and Devine ideal body weight."
>
  <form slot="form" id="calc">
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Patient</legend>
      <div class="field-grid">
        <Field label="Age (years)" name="age" placeholder="70" />
        <div class="field">
          <label for="sex">Sex</label>
          <select id="sex" name="sex">
            <option value="male" selected>Male</option>
            <option value="female">Female</option>
          </select>
          <span class="hint">Female multiplies the numerator by 0.85.</span>
        </div>
        <Field
          label="Serum creatinine (mg/dL)"
          name="scr"
          placeholder="1.2"
          hint="US coursework uses mg/dL. If you were given µmol/L, convert first."
        />
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset>
      <legend>Size</legend>
      <div class="field-grid">
        <Field label="Weight" name="weight" placeholder="70" />
        <div class="field">
          <label for="weightUnit">Weight unit</label>
          <select id="weightUnit" name="weightUnit">
            <option value="kg" selected>Kilograms (kg)</option>
            <option value="lb">Pounds (lb)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <Field
          label="Height"
          name="height"
          placeholder="70"
          hint="Needed for Devine IBW so it can be compared with actual weight."
        />
        <div class="field">
          <label for="heightUnit">Height unit</label>
          <select id="heightUnit" name="heightUnit">
            <option value="in" selected>Inches (in)</option>
            <option value="cm">Centimeters (cm)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="hint" style="margin-top:-0.6rem">
        Conversions used here: 2.2 lb = 1 kg, and 1 in = 2.54 cm. Feet are left
        out on purpose; convert to inches first if that is what you were given.
        Dosing weight is whichever is lower: actual body weight or ideal body
        weight.
      </p>
    </fieldset>

    <div class="field-actions">
      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Find CrCl</button>
      <button class="btn btn--quiet" type="reset">Clear</button>
    </div>
    <div class="field-actions" style="margin-top:0.9rem">
      <button
        class="btn btn--quiet btn--tiny"
        type="button"
        data-example='{"age":"70","sex":"male","scr":"1.2","weight":"70","weightUnit":"kg","height":"70","heightUnit":"in"}'
      >
        Example: 70 yr male, 70 kg, 70 in, Scr 1.2
      </button>
      <button
        class="btn btn--quiet btn--tiny"
        type="button"
        data-example='{"age":"65","sex":"female","scr":"1.0","weight":"130","weightUnit":"lb","height":"64","heightUnit":"in"}'
      >
        Example: 65 yr female, 130 lb, 64 in, Scr 1.0
      </button>
      <button
        class="btn btn--quiet btn--tiny"
        type="button"
        data-example='{"age":"55","sex":"male","scr":"1.1","weight":"90","weightUnit":"kg","height":"70","heightUnit":"in"}'
      >
        Example: 55 yr male, 90 kg, 5&apos;10&quot;, Scr 1.1
      </button>
    </div>

    <!--
    Adjusted body weight mode (not used this course):
    <div class="modes" role="group" aria-label="Choose which weight to use">
      <button class="mode-btn" type="button" data-mode="adj" aria-pressed="false">
        Adjusted body weight
      </button>
    </div>
    <div data-mode-panel="adj" hidden>
      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Find CrCl with AdjBW</button>
    </div>
    -->
  </form>

  <div slot="concept">
    <h2>Kidney function for dosing math</h2>
    <p>
      Many drug references still dose from estimated creatinine clearance in
      mL/min. Cockcroft-Gault is the equation pharmacy courses lean on for that
      estimate. It is not the same thing as eGFR from a lab report.
    </p>

    <h3>Cockcroft-Gault</h3>
    <pre class="formula">CrCl (mL/min) = [(140 - age) × weight(kg) × sex] / (72 × Scr)

sex = 1 (male) or 0.85 (female)
Scr in mg/dL</pre>
    <p>
      Age is in years. Weight has to be in kilograms before it enters the
      formula. Serum creatinine is the concentration in mg/dL that exams in the
      US usually quote.
    </p>

    <h3>Which weight?</h3>
    <p>
      This course compares actual body weight with Devine ideal body weight and
      uses the lower of the two in Cockcroft-Gault.
    </p>
    <pre class="formula">ABW   = the patient's actual body weight
IBW   = Devine ideal body weight
dosing weight = min(ABW, IBW)</pre>
    <pre class="formula">IBW (male)   = 50 kg + 2.3 kg × (height(in) - 60)
IBW (female) = 45.5 kg + 2.3 kg × (height(in) - 60)</pre>
    <!--
    AdjBW = IBW + 0.4 × (ABW - IBW)
    Not required for this course.
    -->
    <p>
      If the patient weighs less than ideal, actual weight wins. If they weigh
      more than ideal, ideal weight wins. Either way, the calculator shows both
      numbers before it picks.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <strong>Study aid, not a chart order.</strong> Cockcroft-Gault and
        weight-selection rules vary by lecturer and by drug monograph. This
        tool follows the course rule of using the lower of ABW and IBW, and
        shows the algebra with your numbers substituted in.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</CalcPage>

<script>
  import { setupCalculator } from '../../scripts/calc.js';
  import { solveCreatinineClearance } from '../../scripts/solvers/creatinine-clearance.js';

  setupCalculator({
    form: '#calc',
    solve: solveCreatinineClearance,
  });
</script>
